\[\operatorname{div}\mathbf{v}=q_{h},\quad|\mathbf{v}|_{1,\Omega}\leq C_{1}\|q _{h}\|_{0,\Omega}.\] (4.10)

Therefore, since \(M_{h}\subset H^{1}(\Omega)\) we want to construct a function \(\pi_{h}\mathbf{v}\) in \(X_{h}\) that satisfies

\[\sum_{\kappa\in\mathcal{T}_{h}}\int_{\kappa}\pi_{h}\mathbf{v}\cdot\mathbf{grad }\,\mu_{h}\,dx=\sum_{\kappa\in\mathcal{T}_{h}}\int_{\kappa}\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{grad}\,\mu_{h}\,dx\quad\quad\forall\mu_{h}\in M_{h}.\]

